  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Nebraska's 3rd Congressional District, one of the largest and most rural districts in the nation, is holding its general election on November 3, 2026. Incumbent Republican U.S. Rep. Adrian Smith, first elected in 2006 and the longest-serving representative in the district's history, is seeking an 11th term. The sprawling district covers 80 of Nebraska's 93 counties across approximately 70,000 square miles and has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+27, making it one of the most Republican-leaning districts in the country. Smith faces a general election field of four opponents: Democrat Becky Stille, Legal Marijuana NOW candidate David Else, and independent candidates Mark Cohen and Macey Budke, with key issues including agriculture, tariffs, trade policy, immigration, and federal spending.",
